{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:11:23Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 15, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Edit a task title\n2\t\n3\tTaiga #2 \u00b7 consumes `docs/spec.md`\n4\t\n5\t## Conventions established (before designing anything)\n6\t\n7\t- No component library, no icon set, no design tokens file \u2014 plain CSS in\n8\t  `frontend/src/App.css`, function components, hooks only.\n9\t- Existing button style is a single neutral style (`button { border, white\n10\t  bg, radius 5px }`) with no primary/secondary visual hierarchy \u2014 Done and\n11\t  Delete look the same. Nothing today distinguishes \"safe\" vs \"destructive\"\n12\t  by color.\n13\t- Existing form pattern is `AddTask.jsx`: a `<form onSubmit>` wrapping an\n14\t  `<input>` + submit `<button>`, client-side `.trim()` check before calling\n15\t  the handler, `aria-label` on the input.\n16\t- Existing per-row actions (`TaskList.jsx`) are plain-text buttons with an\n17\t  `aria-label` that includes the task's title (`` `Complete ${task.title}` ``)\n18\t  for screen-reader disambiguation between rows.\n19\t- Existing error surface is a single global banner in `App.jsx` \u2014\n20\t  `<p className=\"error\" role=\"alert\">` \u2014 fed by `run()`'s catch block.\n21\t- Existing color tokens in use: text `#16191c`, border `#ccd2d6`, error text\n22\t  `#a3271d` on error bg `#fbe9e7`, muted `#6b7780`, card bg `#fff`, page bg\n23\t  `#f6f7f8`.\n24\t\n25\t**Decision: introduce no new component, no new color, no new button style.**\n26\tEverything below extends `TaskList.jsx` and `App.css` in place, per the\n27\tspec's affected areas.\n28\t\n29\t## Interaction model\n30\t\n31\t`TaskList` owns edit state locally (per spec: \"per-task edit-mode state\"):\n32\t\n33\t```js\n34\tconst [editingId, setEditingId] = useState(null)\n35\tconst [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\n36\tconst [validationError, setValidationError] = useState(null)\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t- **Enter edit mode** \u2014 click a task's `Edit` button \u2192\n40\t  `setEditingId(task.id); setDraft(task.title); setValidationError(null)`.\n41\t  The input autofocuses (`autoFocus` \u2014 safe here since it only fires on a\n42\t  direct user click, not on page load).\n43\t- **Opening edit on a different task** \u2014 clicking `Edit` elsewhere just calls\n44\t  `startEdit` again; `editingId`/`draft` are overwritten, so the previous\n45\t  row's unsaved draft is silently discarded. This *is* the resolution to the\n46\t  spec's open question 2 (only one task edits at a time) \u2014 no confirmation\n47\t  dialog, per the spec's stated default.\n48\t- **Cancel** \u2014 `Cancel` button, or `Escape` in the input \u2192\n49\t  `setEditingId(null); setValidationError(null)`. No request sent. The row\n50\t  re-renders from `tasks` (untouched), so the original title reappears with\n51\t  no extra revert logic needed.\n52\t- **Save, empty/whitespace draft (AC4)** \u2014 submit handler trims the draft\n53\t  first, same as `AddTask.jsx` line 8. If empty, **block before calling\n54\t  `onEdit`**: `setValidationError(\"Title can't be empty.\")`, keep\n55\t  `editingId` set, return. No request is sent, focus stays in the input\n56\t  (it never lost focus), the draft the user typed is preserved so they can\n57\t  fix it in place.\n58\t- **Save, valid draft (AC2)** \u2014 trimmed non-empty value \u2192 close edit mode\n59\t  immediately (`setEditingId(null)`), call `onEdit(task.id, trimmed)`. This\n60\t  is optimistic: the row briefly shows the old title until `App.jsx`'s\n61\t  `run()` \u2192 `refresh()` completes, then shows the new one. No new\n62\t  loading-state UI is introduced for this, matching Complete/Delete, which\n63\t  have the same brief-old-value-until-refresh gap today.\n64\t- **Save, oversized draft (AC5)** \u2014 no client-side length check is added\n65\t  (spec non-goal). An over-200-char draft is *not* caught by the empty\n66\t  check, so it takes the same path as a valid save: edit mode closes\n67\t  optimistically, the request goes out, the backend 422s, and the existing\n68\t  global banner in `App.jsx` shows it \u2014 identical to how `AddTask` handles\n69\t  an oversized create today. This means AC5, unlike AC4, does *not* keep\n70\t  edit mode open on rejection \u2014 that asymmetry is intentional: the spec says\n71\t  AC5 should be rejected \"the same way create rejects it today,\" and create\n72\t  has no such behavior either. If this asymmetry is undesirable, the fix is\n73\t  a client-side length guard, which is explicitly out of scope (non-goal:\n74\t  \"No character counter or other new max-length UI\").\n75\t- **Click elsewhere on the page while editing** \u2014 no effect. Edit mode is\n76\t  not exited by blur/click-outside; only explicit Cancel, Escape, Save, or\n77\t  switching to another row's Edit closes it. (Not specified by the spec;\n78\t  chosen because silent data loss on an accidental click is worse than\n79\t  requiring an explicit action.)\n80\t\n81\t## States (per row)\n82\t\n83\t### Display, open task (unchanged baseline)\n84\t\n85\t```\n86\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n87\t\u2502 Buy milk                     [ Done ] [ Edit ] [Delete] \u2502\n88\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\t`Edit` is inserted between `Done` and `Delete` \u2014 a modifying action sits\n92\tnext to the other modifying action, and stays spatially separated from the\n93\tdestructive one on its far side (`destructive-emphasis` guideline: keep\n94\tdestructive actions visually distinguishable/separated; nothing here changes\n95\tDelete's own styling, just its neighbor).\n96\t\n97\t### Display, done task\n98\t\n99\t```\n100\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n101\t\u2502 S\u0336u\u0336b\u0336m\u0336i\u0336t\u0336 \u0336r\u0336e\u0336p\u0336o\u0336r\u0336t\u0336  (struck through, 0.55 opacity)   [ Edit ] [Delete] \u2502\n102\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\tPer spec open question 1 (default: yes, done tasks stay editable), `Edit`\n106\trenders unconditionally \u2014 only `Done` is conditional on `!task.done`\n107\t(existing behavior, unchanged).\n108\t\n109\t### Edit mode, just opened\n110\t\n111\t```\n112\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n113\t\u2502 [ Buy milk|                    ]   [ Save ] [Cancel]\u2502\n114\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\tInput replaces the `.task-title` span in place (same flex position,\n118\t`flex: 1`). `Save`/`Cancel` replace `Done`/`Edit`/`Delete` in the same slot \u2014\n119\tonly one action set is ever visible per row, so there's no risk of clicking\n120\ta stale Delete mid-edit.\n121\t\n122\t### Edit mode, empty/whitespace submitted (AC4)\n123\t\n124\t```\n125\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n126\t\u2502 [                                ]   [ Save ] [Cancel]\u2502\n127\t\u2502 Title can't be empty.                                \u2502\n128\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n129\t```\n130\t\n131\t- Input gets a `.invalid` class \u2192 border color becomes `#a3271d` (same red\n132\t  as the existing error token). This is a *reinforcing* signal, not the only\n133\t  one (`color-not-only`): the text message is the primary signal and is what\n134\t  a screen reader announces.\n135\t- Error text: `#a3271d` on the card's white background \u2014 **7.33:1**,\n136\t  computed from the actual token (`R163 G39 B29` \u2192 relative luminance\n137\t  0.0933; `(1.0 + 0.05) / (0.0933 + 0.05) = 7.33`). Passes AAA (\u22657:1), well\n138\t  past the 4.5:1 floor.\n139\t- `<p className=\"task-edit-error\" role=\"alert\" id={`edit-error-${task.id}`}>`\n140\t  \u2014 reuses the exact `role=\"alert\"` pattern already in `App.jsx:46`, so it's\n141\t  announced immediately (`aria-live-errors`), rather than inventing a new\n142\t  live-region convention.\n143\t- Input carries `aria-invalid=\"true\"` and\n144\t  `aria-describedby=\"edit-error-${task.id}\"` while the error is shown\n145\t  (`error-clarity`, `focus-management` adjacent: the field stays focused,\n146\t  nothing moves).\n147\t- Message wording states cause plainly (\"Title can't be empty.\") \u2014 no\n148\t  contrived \"how to fix\" clause needed since the fix is self-evident (type\n149\t  something) and the input is right there, already focused.\n150\t- Layout: the error line uses `flex-basis: 100%; order: 1` inside the same\n151\t  flex row, so it drops below the input/buttons without restructuring the\n152\t  `<li>` into a grid or adding a wrapper element.\n153\t\n154\t### Populated list, mixed states\n155\t\n156\tLong titles: the input is a native single-line text field \u2014 no truncation\n157\tneeded (unlike the read-only span, an editable field scrolls its own\n158\toverflow). No `textarea` \u2014 title is and remains a single-line field per\n159\t`TaskIn`.\n160\t\n161\tOne task / many tasks / all-done / all-open: no new empty-state or\n162\tvirtualization concerns \u2014 this feature touches only the per-row action set,\n163\t`TaskList`'s empty-state branch (`EMPTY_COPY`) is untouched.\n164\t\n165\t### Error from the backend (404 deleted-elsewhere, 422 oversized)\n166\t\n167\tReuses the existing global banner exactly as `AddTask`'s create failures do\n168\ttoday \u2014 no new UI:\n169\t\n170\t```\n171\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n172\t\u2502 request failed (404)                            \u2502  \u2190 .error, role=\"alert\"\n173\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n174\t  Buy milk                     [ Done ] [ Edit ] [Delete]\n175\t```\n176\t\n177\tRow has already reverted to display mode (optimistic close) showing the\n178\tpre-edit title, since `refresh()` re-fetches the unchanged store state.\n179\t\n180\t## Keyboard & accessibility\n181\t\n182\t- **Enter** submits (native form-submit behavior, same as `AddTask` \u2014 no\n183\t  explicit `onKeyDown` needed for this one).\n184\t- **Escape** cancels \u2014 needs an explicit `onKeyDown` on the input, since\n185\t  Escape has no native form behavior:\n186\t  `if (e.key === 'Escape') cancelEdit()`.\n187\t- **Tab order**: Save then Cancel, matching DOM/visual order left-to-right \u2014\n188\t  no `tabIndex` overrides needed.\n189\t- **Focus ring**: rely on the browser default (project sets no `outline:\n190\t  none` anywhere today) \u2014 `focus-states` is satisfied for free.\n191\t- **Touch targets**: Save/Cancel/Edit reuse the existing `button` rule\n192\t  unchanged (`padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem`), same as Done/Delete today. That\n193\t  rule's rendered height is under the 44\u00d744 recommendation project-wide \u2014\n194\t  true for every button in this app already, not something this feature\n195\t  introduces or is scoped to fix (non-goal territory: this cycle extends\n196\t  `.task`, it doesn't redesign the button system). Flagging it here so it's\n197\t  a known, pre-existing characteristic rather than a silent gap.\n198\t- **Row gap**: existing `.task` `gap: 0.5rem` (8px) already satisfies\n199\t  `touch-spacing` between the new buttons \u2014 no change needed.\n200\t- Input `aria-label=\"Task title\"` \u2014 reuses `AddTask.jsx`'s exact label\n201\t  (line 20). Fine to reuse verbatim: only one row is ever in edit mode at a\n202\t  time (assumption 2), so there's never a duplicate-label ambiguity for\n203\t  screen readers at any given moment.\n204\t- `Edit`/`Save`/`Cancel` buttons get `aria-label`s that include the task\n205\t  title, matching the existing `Complete ${task.title}` / `Delete\n206\t  ${task.title}` convention:\n207\t  - `aria-label={`Edit ${task.title}`}`\n208\t  - `aria-label={`Save new title for ${task.title}`}`\n209\t  - `aria-label={`Cancel editing ${task.title}`}`\n210\t\n211\t## Exact code changes\n212\t\n213\t**`frontend/src/api.js`** \u2014 add next to `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (after\n214\tline 21):\n215\t```js\n216\texport const updateTask = (id, title) =>\n217\t  request(`/api/tasks/${id}`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify({ title }) })\n218\t```\n219\t\n220\t**`frontend/src/App.jsx`** \u2014 add `onEdit` prop to `<TaskList>` (alongside\n221\tlines 54-55), same `run()` wiring as the others:\n222\t```jsx\n223\tonEdit={(id, title) => run(() => api.updateTask(id, title))}\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\t**`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`** \u2014 replace the static\n227\t`task-title` span (line 15) and the fixed action-button block (lines 16-23)\n228\twith a conditional: display mode (current markup, plus the new `Edit`\n229\tbutton) vs. edit mode (form with input + Save/Cancel + optional error line),\n230\tswitched on `task.id === editingId`. State and handlers as described in\n231\t\"Interaction model\" above.\n232\t\n233\t**`frontend/src/App.css`** \u2014 add after the `.task-title` rules (after line\n234\t31):\n235\t```css\n236\t.task-edit-input {\n237\t  flex: 1;\n238\t  min-width: 0;\n239\t  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;\n240\t  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n241\t  border-radius: 5px;\n242\t  font: inherit;\n243\t}\n244\t.task-edit-input.invalid { border-color: #a3271d; }\n245\t.task-edit-error {\n246\t  flex-basis: 100%;\n247\t  order: 1;\n248\t  color: #a3271d;\n249\t  font-size: 0.85rem;\n250\t  margin: 0.3rem 0 0;\n251\t}\n252\t```\n253\tNo changes to `button` \u2014 Edit/Save/Cancel inherit the existing global rule\n254\t(lines 16-23) unstyled, same as Done/Delete.\n255\t\n256\t## Traceability\n257\t\n258\t| AC | Design element |\n259\t|----|-----------------|\n260\t| 1. Enter edit mode | `Edit` button \u2192 `startEdit()` \u2192 input replaces span, pre-filled, autofocused |\n261\t| 2. Save valid edit | Save/Enter \u2192 trimmed non-empty \u2192 `onEdit(id, trimmed)` via `run()`, edit mode closes |\n262\t| 3. Cancel discards | Cancel/Escape \u2192 `setEditingId(null)`, no request, row re-renders from untouched `tasks` |\n263\t| 4. Empty rejected, correctable in place | Client-side trim check blocks the request; `.task-edit-error`, `role=\"alert\"`, `aria-invalid`/`aria-describedby`; edit mode stays open, input keeps focus and draft |\n264\t| 5. Oversized rejected | No client length check (non-goal); 422 surfaces via existing global `.error` banner, same path as `AddTask` create failures today |\n265\t| 6-8. Backend behavior | No UI surface beyond the above \u2014 covered by `updateTask()`'s use of the existing `request()` error handling |\n266\t\n267\t## Non-goals honored\n268\t\n269\tNo new component file, no new color, no new button visual style, no\n270\tcharacter counter, no undo/history UI, no multi-row edit UI, no click-\n271\toutside-to-save/cancel behavior invented beyond what's needed for AC3/AC4.\n272\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NZsyyTrLveyZCNec3bJJss", "session_id": "f0526499-5d58-4d8f-9afb-d01f164ed669"}}
